  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug: `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now returns a value inside the range. `tests/test_types.py` and `tests/test_info_dict.py` pass (71 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Before, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returned `-1`. It now returns `1`.\n- **Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_types.py`, `-5` \u2192 `1` with `min_open` and `20` \u2192 `9` with `max_open`. I did not run them against the old code, so I haven't confirmed they fail without the fix.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
